OL,3,AOxford museum returns ancestral Naga
OL,4,Askulls to India
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe University of Oxford has returned
OL,7,Fthe remains of 39 people taken from the
OL,8,FNaga community during British colonial
OL,9,Frule in India.
OL,11,FA delegation of around 30 people from
OL,12,FNagaland, a mountainous state in
OL,13,Fnorth-eastern India, attended a
OL,14,Fceremony at Oxford's Pitt Rivers Museum
OL,15,Fon Monday to mark the handover.
OL,17,FThe remains, most of which are skulls,
OL,18,Fwill be taken back to India and given
OL,19,Fwhat Naga tribal leaders have described
OL,20,Fas a "respectful rest". There are plans
OL,21,Fto bury them under a joint memorial in
OL,22,Fa park in Nagaland.
OL,23,APub: 10-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
